 {"name": "Freedom for God", "who": "Much Jewish tradition; most Christian theology", "view": "The goal of the Exodus is not independence but covenant: freedom from Pharaoh in order to serve God and live by his law. Political freedom without that becomes a new slavery.", "evidence": "'Let my people go, that they may serve me' (8:1); the march leads to Sinai; the people's longing for Egypt."},
 {"name": "A spiritual pattern", "who": "Origen; much Christian devotion; Gregory of Nyssa, The Life of Moses", "view": "The Exodus is a picture of the soul's journey from sin to God: Egypt is sin, the sea is baptism, the desert is the testing of faith, Canaan is heaven.", "evidence": "1 Corinthians 10:1–11 ('these things happened to them as examples'); the spirituals' double meaning."}
